From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:58:10 -0400
Subject: feat: Peek explains itself, and sync says what folder to pick

Peek's default is Arc's, a click on a pinned tab's link to another site,
so someone who skipped the welcome flow met it unexplained. The first
peeks a profile opens now carry a one-line note at the top of the page:
what a peek is, that Open as Tab keeps the page, and a link to the
setting. Got it, the link, the close box, Open as Tab and Open in Split
View answer it; answered, it never shows again, and unanswered it shows
on at most three peeks. It does not follow a kept page into the window
(peek P19). The welcome flow's question now says what a peek is and
names the last choice "Never peek" (welcome W16).

Sync through a folder has no provider to choose: the user's own sync
app carries the file. The row now says to pick a folder iCloud Drive,
OneDrive, Dropbox, Google Drive or a share keeps, and a folder in the
home folder that none of them keeps gets a note (sidebar-file Sf42,
GitHub issue 38's follow-up).

Why: the owner, 2026-10-26.
Removable when: never; to be folded into the patches that own the code.
